# NOTICE

`Point_Graphics_Signatures.xtf` sourced unmodified from
`https://github.com/MediaComem/FGDM4GS`, path
`WP2-WP3/model/symbology/Point_Graphics_Signatures.xtf`. The repo has no
declared license (`license: null` via the GitHub API, checked
2026-09-12). The report and this repo share an author with this
project's own maintainer - vendored here as real, author-confirmed
corpus material for testing `SIGN BASKET` data resolution (`Sign :=
{name}` -> real `.xtf` object), not redistributed for any other purpose.

Real `SIGN BASKET StandardSymbology.StandardSigns` data: a `Color`
library (`white`/`black`, LCh), a text `Font`/`FontSymbol` pair (an
external TTF-based glyph symbol, `Tree`/`TreeClip`), and one `SymbolSign`
(`ili:Name = Symbol`, `tid=2001`) referencing `Color`/`Symbol`/
`ClipSymbol` by `ili:ref` within the same basket - exercises the exact
wire shape `convert/cartosym.py::SignLibrary` resolves against.

`roadsexgm2ien/RoadsExgm2ien.ili`/`RoadsExgm2ien_Symbols.xtf` (2026-09-12):
same source/provenance as above (`FGDM4GS`, `WP2-WP3/model/symbology/`) -
the INTERLIS reference manual's own canonical `GRAPHIC` example (eCH-0031
§2.16/§3.15.x), 5 `GRAPHIC`s covering all 4 `StandardSymbology` interfaces
(`SurfaceSign`/`PolylineSign`/`TextSign`/`SymbolSign`), paired with a real
`SIGN BASKET` data file (`RoadsExgm2ien_Symbols.xtf`, refman Appendix E) -
the first REAL (not hand-built) `.ili`/`.xtf` pair exercising this whole
pipeline end to end, used by `interlis convert-sld` (`cmd_convert_sld`,
`cli.py`) and `tests/test_convert_cartosym_graphic_to_style.py`/
`tests/test_cli_convert_sld.py`.
`roadsexgm2ien_repo/` holds its base models, resolved via `--repo`
(RULE #9): `RoadsExdm2ben.ili`/`RoadsExdm2ien.ili` fetched from
`https://models.interlis.ch/refhb24/` (the official INTERLIS models
catalog - the reference manual's own companion example models, openly
published for reuse) ; `StandardSymbology.ili`/`AbstractSymbology.ili`
likewise, same catalog/URL prefix (not from FGDM4GS - those are the
official upstream originals FGDM4GS itself imports).

`Surface_Hatching_Stipples_GS.xtf` (2026-09-13): same source/provenance
as `Point_Graphics_Signatures.xtf` above (`FGDM4GS`,
`WP2-WP3/model/symbology/`) - a real `SurfaceSign` ("fill") with a
`HatchSymb` reference to a `PolylineSign` ("continuous") and a
`HatchOffset`, used by `tests/test_convert_cartosym_hatch.py` to verify
`surface_sign_object_to_hatch_pattern` end to end.

`square_diamond_symbols.xtf`: synthetic (not corpus-sourced) `SIGN
BASKET` data - straight-segment `FontSymbol_Surface` symbols (an
axis-aligned square, a diamond, an oblong rectangle, an SE-proportioned
triangle and a flatter one) exercising
`font_symbol_geometry_to_polygon_graphics`. Hand-built because no
vendored corpus `.xtf` carries a polygonal mark of a single shape; the
marks themselves are real (Sachplan Asyl's published SLD uses a
`diamond` and a `triangle` `se:Mark`).

`pattern_x_symbols.xtf`: synthetic (not corpus-sourced) `SIGN BASKET`
data - an X (pycartosym's canonical diagonal cross, started at another
vertex), a triangle pointing right, and a `LineStyle_Pattern` repeating
the X along a line, exercising the well-known shape matcher and
`LineStyle_Pattern`. The marks themselves are real: Sachplan
Übertragungsleitungen's published SLD repeats a WESP X along its lines
and draws a right-pointing arrow on its points.
